actice,--that whether they eat, or drink, or whatsoever they do, to do it all with an habitual aim to the glory of God; by considering his precepts, and the propriety, expediency, appearance, and tendency of their actions.</p>\n<p>ye eat. 7:34; De 12:7,12,18; Ne 8:16-18; Zec 7:5,6; Lu 11:41 Col 3:17,23; 1Pe 4:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-10-32","title":"1 Corinthians 10:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>none. 33; 8:13; Ro 14:13; 2Co 6:3; Php 1:10 Gentiles. or, Greeks. the church. 11:22; Ac 20:28; 1Ti 3:5,15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-1co-10-33","title":"1 Corinthians 10:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"1CO","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>24; 9:19-23; Ro 15:2,3; 2Co 11:28,29; 12:19</p>"}]}